checkers: unknown command `frobnicate`

checkers — the Checkers build tool

USAGE:
    checkers check|run|build|stage|parse ...         run the compiler, `ckc` (see `ckc --help`)
    checkers fmt [--check] [PATH]...                 format .ck files (see `checkers fmt --help`)
    checkers fmt -                                   format standard input
    checkers lsp                                     the language server, on standard input and output
    checkers doc DIR -o OUT                          a package's documentation, as Markdown and HTML
    checkers site SRC -o OUT                         the site: Markdown pages, as Markdown and HTML
    checkers --version

In a directory with checkers.json, the compiler commands first fetch the package's
dependencies and update checkers.lock; the file defaults to main.ck.
`ckc` is found through CKC, else next to `checkers`, else on PATH.
-- exit 2
$ checkers fmt --check tests/fmt/basics.ck tests/fmt/blanks.ck
-- stdout
tests/fmt/basics.ck
tests/fmt/blanks.ck
-- stderr
-- exit 1
$ checkers fmt --check --check
-- stdout
-- stderr
usage: checkers fmt [--check] [PATH]...
       checkers fmt -

Formats each .ck file under each PATH (default: the current directory) in place.
--check changes nothing: it lists the files that would change, and fails if
there are any. `-` formats standard input to standard output.
-- exit 2
$ checkers trust examples/wc.ck
-- stdout
-- stderr
checkers: unknown command `trust`

checkers — the Checkers build tool

USAGE:
    checkers check|run|build|stage|parse ...         run the compiler, `ckc` (see `ckc --help`)
    checkers fmt [--check] [PATH]...                 format .ck files (see `checkers fmt --help`)
    checkers fmt -                                   format standard input
    checkers lsp                                     the language server, on standard input and output
    checkers doc DIR -o OUT                          a package's documentation, as Markdown and HTML
    checkers site SRC -o OUT                         the site: Markdown pages, as Markdown and HTML
